*** Changes to Payslip Editor ***
- Buttons to change month
- Add the net hourly wage (net pay / total hours)
- Net pay is always in the bottom and gross pay is always in the top
- Custom lines default placement: New deduction lines are placed after subtotal(after tax), addition lines are placed just under gross pay
- Automatic recalculation after each change (when creating/removing or moving a custom line.) -- remove the manual recalculate button.

- In the navbar, color the page you are currently on, to help with navigation / knowing where you are

- Implementation question: I don't understand the payroll / generate period page. The payslip editor was created in order to adjust for additions/deductions on the payslip that would change the net amount. This would also help with singular month bonusses or variable bonusses, but I do not understand the payroll page.

*** Changes to workplace calendar: ***
- Work shifts for days that are before the start or after the end of the payroll period should be greyed out on the calendar. -- just like on the planning calendar
- When clicking the calendar, currently it opens a modal, i would like this to appear as a pop-up just over the date you clicked (like the pick-workplace-popup on the planning calendar)
- If no work shifts are already on the current day, it should automatically open the dialogue to add a new shift
- There should be a date field, so you can change it if you click the wrong date
- At the top of the add work shift form, there should be a small banner showing which workplace you are adding a shift for.
- In the add work shift form, it should show the shift time in minutes and decimal with and without the break
- When you are done adding a work shift, you should be returned to the workplace dashboard, not the main dashboard.

- In the workplace settings, there should be a break policy configuration, where you can pick:
-- Break time is paid
-- Break time is static (ie you can only enter yes/no in the work shift configuration, and the break numbers are static)
-- Break time is variable and should be entered manually every time (like it is now)

*** SMTP Implementation ***
Allow the system to send out calender invites to my work emails and add to my Google Calendar.
- IMPORTANT: This whole system should be optional and disableable.
- Add a calendar/SMTP settings page.
- Basic calendar event with title, time, location(verify this against a free api?)
- Configure a default event configuration for each workplace:
- - Change the custom title which is ("På arbejde hos [workplace name]" for on-site and "Arbejder hjemme, [workplace name]" for remote)
- - Change which emails are recipients
- - Change the address for on-site / remote (the default remote address is set globally) --> maybe you are prompted to enter the address already when creating/editing the workplace (optional field in the form)
- Change settings for the connector with easy configuration for cloud providers (just start with gmail)
- - There should be a test button that checks: is the connection ok and without errors
- The system should not care about replies to the events or anything.

